@status active
// axis2_second_loop.spec.vsm — AXIS 2: the SECOND autonomous control loop (lyapunov drift-correction).
// author: Claude/Fable [O] 2026-07-03. Gate: AXIS 1 done (lyapunov calibrated) + loop 1 (S3 alloc) ratified.
// Frame: calibration_autonomy_strategy.vsm · axis2_first_loop.spec.vsm (next_loops → this).
// @status active (epistemic). transform: move — PH-11 move carries content
// VERBATIM (¬compressed); density N/A per revision_plan move_vs_migrate. Over
// target BY DESIGN, declared (2026-08-09).

spec(AXIS2-SECOND-LOOP) {

  insight(ASHBY):
    "Requisite Variety says a regulator meets disturbance variety in exactly TWO ways: AMPLIFY its own
     regulatory capacity, or ATTENUATE the incoming variety. Loop 1 (S3 alloc) is the AMPLIFIER (grant
     resources). This loop is the ATTENUATOR (throttle the input variety). Together they are the two halves
     of Ashby's law made autonomous — the Cyberfilter (attenuate) + the Cyberamplifier (amplify)."

  the_router:   // the elegant payoff — margin_binding IS the decision variable
    "WHICH lever to pull is told by margin_binding (the constraint-name diagnostic — the one DS thought was a
     'useless string'). When the trajectory DIVERGES:
       - margin_binding == 'budget ∈ [0,1]'  → it is a CAPACITY problem → AMPLIFY (defer to loop 1, grant).
       - margin_binding == anything else (or diverging with budget slack) → it is a VARIETY problem →
         ATTENUATE (this loop). The diagnostic label routes between the two loops."

  the_loop(S4_DRIFT_CORRECTION):
    gate: "lyapunov is CALIBRATED (Axis-1: mean_l moves, regime discriminates). Today Diverging only EMITS
           an algedonic (detection). Axis 2 = close it with a tactical S4 attenuation."
    cycle: [
      "DETECT   — regime == Diverging (the calibrated lyapunov certificate: above core, not contracting) for
                  DIVERGE_TICKS consecutive ticks (debounced — don't react to a single tick).",
      "ROUTE    — read margin_binding. budget-bound → HAND OFF to loop 1 (amplify) and do nothing here.
                  else → this loop (attenuate).",
      "DECIDE   — attenuation step: widen the S2 coordination debounce / throttle the ingest admission rate
                  (reduce the rate of admitted perturbations) by ATTEN_STEP.",
      "ACT      — apply the tactical parameter (S4→S2). A5 gate holds: NO lifecycle, NO covenant change; a
                  reversible tactical knob only.",
      "VERIFY   — regime returns to Contracting / InRecurrentSet for RECOVER_TICKS.",
      "REVERT   — restore the normal ingest/debounce when stable; log the whole loop to the S3* audit chain.",
    ]

  guardrails(R10.1):
    [ "CALIBRATED-SIGNAL GATE — act only on the calibrated lyapunov regime (passed Axis-1).",
      "COVENANT FLOOR — attenuation never drops below MIN_ADMIT (never starve the system of its own inputs).",
      "S3* AUDIT — every attenuate/restore recorded on the audit chain.",
      "ESCALATION DUTY — still Diverging after ESCALATE_TICKS at max attenuation → emit algedonic + HOLD +
                         escalate to human (the divergence is not variety-driven and not capacity-driven → novel).",
      "NO DOUBLE-PULL — loop 1 and loop 2 are mutually exclusive per tick (the router guarantees it)." ]

  policy_defaults:  // Claude/Fable recommended — for rmw3 ratification:
    { DIVERGE_TICKS:  "5 (debounce: only act after 5 consecutive diverging ticks)",
      ATTEN_STEP:     "reduce admit rate 20% per step (multiplicative)",
      MIN_ADMIT:      "never below 40% of nominal ingest (covenant floor — don't blind the system)",
      RECOVER_TICKS:  "10 in-recurrent-set ticks before reverting",
      ESCALATE_TICKS: "20 ticks still diverging at max attenuation → escalate (novel divergence)" }

  impl: {
    "1 [S]": "add the Diverging→route→attenuate loop (reuse the lyapunov_diverging detection already emitted).",
    "2 [S]": "the attenuation lever: the S2 debounce / ingest admission-rate knob (reversible tactical param).",
    "3 [S]": "route on margin_binding (budget → hand to loop 1; else → attenuate). Mutual exclusion per tick.",
    "4 [S]": "S3* audit + the ESCALATE_TICKS path (algedonic + hold).",
  }

  acceptance:
    "on sustained Diverging with budget slack, the nucleus autonomously attenuates its input variety and the
     regime returns to contracting; on Diverging WITH budget pressure it defers to loop 1 (amplify); a novel
     divergence (neither) escalates. Ashby's law is now closed autonomously in BOTH directions."

  // ── PHASE 2 (rmw3 2026-07-04) — the REAL attenuator: aggregation, not dropping ──
  phase_2(S2_AGGREGATION_ATTENUATOR): {
    v1_status: "SHIPPED 2026-07-04 (DS): admit_rate scales loop-1 GRANTS down under divergence. This is a
                legitimate SAFETY ('don't amplify into a diverging state') but it is NOT the Ashby attenuator —
                it dampens the amplifier's RESPONSE, it does not attenuate the input VARIETY. Rename its role
                honestly = the amplifier brake.",
    the_problem_with_dropping:
      "the naive attenuator (admit only X% of events, drop the rest) is WRONG for a viability monitor: dropping
       input attenuates the very SIGNAL the system needs to sense trouble — it goes 'calm' by going BLIND. Beer's
       Cyberfilter was never 'see less'; it was 'see the same information at lower variety' — AGGREGATE / SUMMARISE /
       DEBOUNCE, lossless of signal.",
    the_real_lever:
      "widen the S2 coordination DEBOUNCE (the mechanism from ITEM_18, already live across the 80 nodes) under
       sustained divergence: collapse redundant / high-frequency events into summaries → lower variety, SAME
       information. A real sustained change still passes the debounce; only redundant chatter is collapsed. This
       is the attenuation my own impl item 2 originally intended and v1 deferred.",
    guardrail: "a MAX_DEBOUNCE ceiling (the analogue of MIN_ADMIT): never so aggregated that a real excursion is
                hidden. Validate BEFORE trusting: exercise a divergence and confirm widening the debounce speeds
                re-contraction WITHOUT masking a genuine excursion (the instrument_calibration_loop discipline).",
    impl: {
      "P2.1 [S]": "wire loop2 to widen the S2 debounce window (not just admit_rate) under divergence, bounded by MAX_DEBOUNCE.",
      "P2.2 [S]": "keep the v1 admit_rate as the amplifier-brake (complementary); the two compose.",
      "P2.3 [S]": "validation exercise: drive a divergence, confirm re-contraction improves AND no real excursion is masked.",
    },
    owner: "DS [S]. Frame ratified by rmw3 2026-07-04 (aggregation not dropping). policy MAX_DEBOUNCE: Fable to
            propose a default with the ITEM_18 debounce baseline; low-risk tuning."
  }

  next_loops: "after this: the beacon-attested onboarding loop (a new S1 self-onboards when its instruments
               pass Axis-1) — the recursion, ITEM-21. That is where autonomy becomes DISTRIBUTED."
  owner: "Claude/Fable [O] (this design) → DS [S] impl. rmw3 (S5): ratify policy_defaults + the attenuation lever."
  status: "RATIFIED 2026-07-04 — policy_defaults locked as proposed (DIVERGE_TICKS=5, ATTEN_STEP=20%,
           MIN_ADMIT=40%, RECOVER_TICKS=10, ESCALATE_TICKS=20). → DS [S] impl. No further rmw3 gate."
}


